        "original_id": "ae3cf163-fe18-5ee3-96d3-1bb8361e5e3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Connors, Leon Danielian, Alec Guinness, Robert Redford\n- Works: Mannix, Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious\n- Roles: actor, private detective character, ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, educator\n- Awards: Golden Globe Award, Emmy nominations\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Danielian was born on 31 October 1920 and was an American ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, and educator.\n- Mike Connors was born Krekor Ohanian on August 15, 1925, and he was an Armenian-American actor.\n- Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious is a 1965 comedy film starring Alec Guinness, Mike Connors, and Robert Redford.\n- From 1967 to 1975, Mike Connors played private detective Joe Mannix in the CBS television series Mannix.\n- In 1970, Mike Connors won a Golden Globe Award for Mannix, the first of six straight nominations.\n- From 1970 through 1973, Mike Connors received four consecutive Emmy nominations for Mannix.\n- Leon Danielian died on 8 March 1997.\n- Mike Connors died on January 26, 2017.",
